{
  "version": "tactical-v4-weapon-models",
  "status": "design_for_native_integration_after_20261115_user_correction",
  "scope": "Original accelerated-game design for 22 personas. Every company has fixed insertion transport. MCP-022/103/087/027/006 have exactly one independently controlled combat vehicle per company plus their existing finite female bodies; no extra pilot body is granted. Final native export remains the only runtime authority. Published historical/v2 runs remain frozen.",
  "contract": {
    "id": "lowercase mcpNNN_family; stable unit_id + family_id key",
    "ammo_capacity": "Total projectile rounds including the initial loaded magazine, not reserve plus magazine. Initial reserve = ammo_capacity - magazine_capacity; no free top-up.",
    "burst_interval_s": "Last shot of completed burst to first shot of next burst; not first-to-first.",
    "after_empty_magazine": "Next shot at max(last-shot cadence due, reload completion). Do not add both delays. Reset incomplete burst after reload. A final partial burst spends and fires only rounds actually present.",
    "simulation": "Exactly 10 Hz. All authored fire_interval_s, burst_interval_s and magazine_reload_s are positive whole 0.1 s intervals. One body/platform emits at most one actual projectile per tick; no hidden rounding or sub-frame fire.",
    "budget": "Per-body/per-platform unarmored raw sustained damage including full-magazine reload must be 80-120% of old family damage/reload_s; total inventory raw damage 80-120%. Accuracy, armor, cover and AoE target count are not folded into this accounting. Vehicle quantity is intentionally corrected from per-body phantom vehicles to one actual platform per company; do not multiply a platform model's budget by the body count. New demolition has an explicit grenade reference, not a claim that the old medic/engineer damage budget was preserved.",
    "accuracy_scale": "Multiplicative model-level accuracy modifier; inherit existing family curve and moving/close penalties. Clamp using the existing model. Does not create a second hit roll.",
    "skill_ammo": "Approved by root: one actual projectile consumes one actual round plus one finite skill charge. Skill obeys the actual magazine, reload, cadence and projectile capacity checks.",
    "resupply": "Actual source rounds and recipient deficits conserved; replenishment does not complete reload or reset next-fire time. No automatic free refill when converting legacy family IDs or saving/replaying.",
    "fire_mode": "Only single or burst. For single, burst_size=1 and fire_interval_s=burst_interval_s; magazine reload remains independent.",
    "mean_fire_interval_s": "Full-magazine first shot to next full-magazine first shot cycle divided by magazine_capacity; this is a sustained-rate design expectation under neutral haste, not projectile damage after accuracy/armor. For a magazine not divisible by burst size, account for its actual partial final burst and reset after reload; never extend the burst or discard rounds. Final inventory magazine may be partial and fires only real remaining rounds.",
    "entity_separation": "Exactly one independent tank/APV/SPG/attack helicopter per designated company. The existing finite bodies have separate rifles/carbines/pistols and ammo. Vehicles use the same persona shared consciousness (min_crew=0); no extra pilot or body is spawned. Seats contain only existing bodies, and all may disembark while the vehicle remains.",
    "fixed_transport": "All 22 personas have one fixed insertion transport and fixed recovery transport; per-sortie transport selectors are removed. Multiple actual boats may be required by a fixed boat capacity. Published saved runs are not silently remapped.",
    "support_revision": "MCP-116 supply_network is a temporary reload/protection buff, with no reserve-pool transfer or free ammo. Ordinary gun magazines/reserves remain finite.",
    "tank_passengers": "MCP-022 tank passenger capacity is zero. Its six rifle bodies remain independent accompanying infantry. Fixed heavy lander carries one tank plus six existing bodies; tank control never creates a pilot body."
  },
